From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:32:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nb/intel/haswell/native_raminit: The eye after the 2D
 centring in its units

data_time_centering_2d() keeps the margins of each Vref point in
tenths of a tick, as get_ber_margin_byte() gives them, and after the
centring of a byte it moves them by the shift it applied: calc, the
shift in ticks times 10, is already in those units, and the code added
calc * 10, ten times the shift. The margins of one side then reach the
clamp at 0, which changes their sum, the average margin with which the
per-bit pass places the byte before it walks each bit, and the margins
stored in the results.

Add calc itself.

TEST=Build of the ThinkPad W541 with the native RAM init.

Change-Id: Ief828bbfdf12221d426e90f5708a7e17745533d1
---
 .../intel/haswell/native_raminit/train_2d_margins.c          | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/train_2d_margins.c b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/train_2d_margins.c
index 979e3e0f10..4d7a196910 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/train_2d_margins.c
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/train_2d_margins.c
@@ -337,11 +337,12 @@ void data_time_centering_2d(
 						en_rx_duty_cycle);
 					for (uint8_t vref = 0; vref < ARRAY_SIZE(vref_points);
 										vref++) {
+						/* The margins are in tenths of a tick, as calc */
 						const int32_t calc = *c_sum * 10;
 						const int32_t max = MAX_POSSIBLE_TIME * 10;
 						uint32_t *eye = eye_shape[vref][channel][byte];
-						eye[0] = clamp_s32(0, eye[0] + calc * 10, max);
-						eye[1] = clamp_s32(0, eye[1] - calc * 10, max);
+						eye[0] = clamp_s32(0, eye[0] + calc, max);
+						eye[1] = clamp_s32(0, eye[1] - calc, max);
 						if (!en_2d)
 							break;
 					}
